# Web feature architecture

Every feature under `web/src/features/<name>/` follows this layout:

```
features/<name>/
├── store/<name>.store.ts           # Zustand state + patch/reset only
├── orchestration/<name>.orchestrator.ts  # Logic; calls repo, store, chrome
├── hooks/use-<name>-screen.ts      # React: subscribe, lifecycle, routing
├── repo/<name>.repo.ts             # Supabase RPC only
├── ui/<name>-screen.tsx            # Presentational; uses hook
├── <name>.routes.tsx
└── index.ts
```

## Rules

- **Store**: serializable UI state, `patch`, `reset`. No RPC, no `navigate`, no toasts.
- **Orchestration**: async work, error handling, patching store. Returns hints (`needsOpener`, `matchId`) — not side effects.
- **Hook**: `usePlayStore` + effects (poll, realtime, redirect). Passes orchestrator methods to UI.
- **Repo**: `callRpc` only. No React, no Zustand.
- **UI**: render + event handlers via hook. No direct repo/store/orchestrator imports.

## Reference

`features/play/` is the canonical example.

Do not add `controller/` folders. Rename to `orchestration/` + `hooks/`.
